{
 "format": "maxbook",
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Welcome to Maxbook",
 "cells": [
  {
   "id": "w01",
   "type": "markdown",
   "source": "# Welcome to Maxbook\n\nMaxbook is a notebook for **literate computing with Maxima**: prose, formulas and live computations in one document. Text cells are Markdown with LaTeX math, such as $e^{i\\pi}+1=0$ or\n\n$$\\int_0^\\infty e^{-x^2}\\,dx = \\frac{\\sqrt{\\pi}}{2}.$$\n\nPress **Shift+Enter** to run a cell, **Ctrl+K** to search commands and templates, and **Run all** to recompute the whole document."
  },
  {
   "id": "w02",
   "type": "markdown",
   "source": "## Maxima cells\n\nA Maxima cell holds ordinary Maxima input. Each displayed result gets its `%o` label, and you can copy it as LaTeX or as Maxima text."
  },
  {
   "id": "w03",
   "type": "code",
   "source": "f(x) := x^2 * sin(x)$\nintegrate(f(x), x);\ndiff(f(x), x, 2);",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "kind": "result",
     "label": "%o2",
     "latex": "2\\,x\\,\\sin x+\\left(2-x^2\\right)\\,\\cos x",
     "text": "2*x*sin(x)+(2-x^2)*cos(x)"
    },
    {
     "kind": "result",
     "label": "%o3",
     "latex": "-\\left(x^2\\,\\sin x\\right)+2\\,\\sin x+4\\,x\\,\\cos x",
     "text": "-(x^2*sin(x))+2*sin(x)+4*x*cos(x)"
    }
   ],
   "inputs": [
    1,
    2,
    3
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "w04",
   "type": "markdown",
   "source": "## Math cells\n\nA math cell is edited as a formula. Type a word such as `int`, `frac`, `sum`, `lim` or `matrix` and pick a template; **Tab** jumps between the empty boxes. The Maxima translation is shown under the formula, so you always see what will be evaluated."
  },
  {
   "id": "w05",
   "type": "math",
   "source": "integrate(sin(x)/x, x, 0, inf);",
   "latex": "\\int_{0}^{\\infty}\\frac{\\sin x}{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "kind": "result",
     "label": "%o4",
     "latex": "\\frac{\\pi}{2}",
     "text": "%pi/2"
    }
   ],
   "inputs": [
    4
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "w06",
   "type": "math",
   "source": "sum(1/k^2, k, 1, inf);",
   "latex": "\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{k^2}",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "kind": "result",
     "label": "%o5",
     "latex": "\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty }{\\frac{1}{k^2}}",
     "text": "'sum(1/k^2,k,1,inf)"
    }
   ],
   "inputs": [
    5
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "w07",
   "type": "code",
   "source": "/* simpsum evaluates the symbolic sum above */\nsum(1/k^2, k, 1, inf), simpsum;",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "kind": "result",
     "label": "%o6",
     "latex": "\\frac{\\pi^2}{6}",
     "text": "%pi^2/6"
    }
   ],
   "inputs": [
    6
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "w08",
   "type": "markdown",
   "source": "## Linear algebra\n\nMatrices typed in a math cell become Maxima `matrix(...)` objects."
  },
  {
   "id": "w09",
   "type": "math",
   "source": "A: matrix([2, 1], [1, 3]);",
   "latex": "A\\coloneq\\begin{pmatrix}2 & 1\\\\ 1 & 3\\end{pmatrix}",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "kind": "result",
     "label": "%o7",
     "latex": "\\begin{pmatrix} 2&1\\\\ 1&3\\end{pmatrix}",
     "text": "matrix([2,1],[1,3])"
    }
   ],
   "inputs": [
    7
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "w10",
   "type": "code",
   "source": "eigenvalues(A);\nA^^-1;",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "kind": "result",
     "label": "%o8",
     "latex": "\\left[ \\left[ -\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}-5}{2}\\right) , \\frac{\\sqrt{5}+5}{2} \\right]  , \\left[ 1 , 1 \\right]  \\right]",
     "text": "[[-((sqrt(5)-5)/2),(sqrt(5)+5)/2],[1,1]]"
    },
    {
     "kind": "result",
     "label": "%o9",
     "latex": "\\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{3}{5}&-\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)\\\\ -\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)&\\frac{2}{5}\\end{pmatrix}",
     "text": "matrix([3/5,-(1/5)],[-(1/5),2/5])"
    }
   ],
   "inputs": [
    8,
    9
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "w11",
   "type": "markdown",
   "source": "## Inline plots\n\n`iplot2d`, `iplot3d`, `idraw2d` and `idraw3d` take the same arguments as `plot2d`, `plot3d`, `draw2d` and `draw3d`, and draw into the notebook. Worksheets written for wxMaxima keep working: `wxplot2d` and friends are aliases."
  },
  {
   "id": "w12",
   "type": "code",
   "source": "iplot2d([sin(x), cos(2*x)/2], [x, -2*%pi, 2*%pi])$",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "kind": "image",
